\f1\fs22 The smell of lime from the dank concrete caught in Eloise\'92s throat. More than once she considered carrying her shoes. Alexander studied everything like it was a film location. Sarah tried to hold her belly in. Hayley\'92s wrist ached from holding the gun to Alexander\'92s head.\
\'93Is that still necessary?\'94 Alexander complained.\
Hayley shoved him and he nearly toppled down a flight of stairs; he would have collected Sarah if he\'92d tripped.\
Sarah stopped midway down and turned. \'93Do you promise to behave?\'94 she asked of Alexander.\
\'93I\'92m not the one with the trigger finger.\'94\
Sarah and Hayley exchanged stern looks; Hayley relaxed and pocketed the gun. Kathy picked at her patch.\
\'93I have a story arc in mind,\'94 Sarah told Alexander.\
\'93Oh?\'94 Alexander perked up.\
\'93A shy, reflective family man, caught in a military uprising with his loving wife and family, must draw on his inner strength to exude calm while a guide and a security officer lead them to safety.\'94\
\'93The man sounds like a dweeb,\'94 Alexander remarked.\
\'93He\'92s protecting his loving wife and baby at all costs,\'94 Sarah explained. \'93Quiet now, he\'92s constantly evaluating, holding his light back, surprise hero later.\'94\
Alexander contemplated. \'93I love it. Play my part down now, which sharpens the rise to the call later.\'94\
\'93Exactly.\'94\
\'93Who\'92s she?\'94 Alexander nodded down to Kathy.\
\'93She plays  a doctor,\'94 Sarah said.\
Alexander nodded. \'93I guess she\'92s up to the part.\'94\
\'93She is.\'94\
\'93And what about mother?\'94\
Sarah looked to Eloise. \'93Soon to be grandmother. Proud, loving, protective mother.\'94\
\'93Can you play that part, mother?\'94 Alexander asked Eloise.\
\'93I\'92ll treat it as the role of a lifetime,\'94 Eloise said, picking at the remaining adhesive on her wrists.\
Alexander nodded and said to Sarah, \'93The grandmother part is presumably the character you sacrifice for the pathos.\'94\
\'93Just after the lead falls down a flight of stairs and breaks his neck,\'94 Eloise muttered to herself.\
Sarah took Alexander\'92s hand. \'93Let\'92s just improv it for now.\'94\
Alexander didn\'92t answer.\
\'93Are we good?\'94 Sarah checked.\
Alexander nodded. \'93Already in character. Quiet, reflective, analytical. Allowing others to lead until my reveal of strength in the climax.\'94\
Chip, at the back of the line, kept his mouth shut. Apparently he was an extra, which suited him just fine, as long as the script didn\'92t call him to die in a hail of bullets. It was his feet that were killing him. He could fall down the stairs at any step, and take out everyone underneath him.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Bala led them through narrow passages of exposed pipes and wiring. They passed other maintenance personnel who passed by while failing to be convincing about not recognising anyone. To Eloise, they didn\'92t look like they\'92d taken a side in Alexander\'92s attempted coup.\
At a door to a stairwell, Bala stopped and put a finger to his lips. \'93We\'92re under the office park. Two more doors, and we\'92re at the Traverse station.\'94\
Eloise nodded. \'93If we get to the Ruined Castle end, I can take it from there.\'94\
\'93Sarah needs to rest,\'94 Kathy said.\
\'93She\'92ll get four minutes or so in a Traverse car,\'94 Eloise said, not without sympathy.\
Bala went through the stairwell door, taking care to buffer its shutting so it didn\'92t slam and echo. A minute later he reappeared.\
\'93The Traverse is heavily guarded,\'94 Bala said. \'93They\'92re checking passes and corroborating id.\'94\
\'93Are they mine or the lauded T.V. personaly\'92s?\'94 Eloise asked.\
Bala shrugged. \'93I am just peering through the door. That is all.\'94\
They let an awkward silence fester while everyone avoided saying, 
\f2\i we need a plan.
\f1\i0 \
Sarah faced up to Alexander, who was clearly uncomfortable with the belly bump barrier between them. \'93I hadn\'92t workshopped this part,\'94 she told him. \'93What would you suggest?\'94\
Alexander laid his eyes on each of the group, including the bump. He was about to speak then hesitated. A few moments later: \'93I have a plan.\'94\
They all hated it. Chip proposed a couple of amendments. Bala was happy he had notfurther part to play. When it was all agreed, Hayley made it clear that Alexander would be the first cadaver if anything went wrong.\
